    "id": "text:msg_mockupturn_155:0",
    "kind": "assistant_text",
    "live": false,
    "markdown": "The jitter came from two things: the drag handler wrote every pointer position straight into the layout store, so sub-pixel values fought the CSS width, and nothing clamped the sidebar to a minimum. I clamped the pointer value to `MIN_WIDTH` in `useSidebarDrag.ts`, rounded the stored width in `store.ts`, and added `min-width: 180px` to `sidebar.css`.\n\nTests, lint and typecheck pass. The Vite cache clear was denied by a project rule, which is fine: the dev server picks the change up without it.",
    "messageUuid": "a-mockup-turn-179",
    "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
    "phase": "answer",
    "turnId": "turn:u-mockup-turn-002"
